  ("Using Examples" 0.1429 0.3355 0.3183 0.3526 0.3526 0.0343 0.0059 0.3370 0.0692)
  ("In addition to being an introduction to data science, this book is intended to be useful" 0.1429 0.8571 0.3590 0.3805 0.3805 0.0214 0.0048 0.3033 0.0185)
  ("in discussions of and day-to-day work in the field. Answering a question by citing this" 0.1429 0.8571 0.3781 0.3995 0.3995 0.0214 0.0047 0.3268 0.0170)
  ("book and quoting examples does not require permission. We appreciate, but do not" 0.1428 0.8571 0.3971 0.4185 0.4185 0.0214 0.0065 0.2911 0.0422)
  ("require, attribution. Formal attribution usually includes the title, author, publisher, and" 0.1429 0.8571 0.4162 0.4376 0.4376 0.0214 0.0038 0.3502 0.0652)
  ("ISBN. For example: “Data Science for Business by Foster Provost and Tom Fawcett" 0.1429 0.8571 0.4352 0.4566 0.4566 0.0214 0.0075 0.2738 0.0495)
  ("(O’Reilly). Copyright 2013 Foster Provost and Tom Fawcett, 978-1-449-36132-7.”" 0.1429 0.8168 0.4543 0.4757 0.4757 0.0214 0.0047 0.3184 0.0861)
  ("If you feel your use of examples falls outside fair use or the permission given above, feel" 0.1429 0.8571 0.4824 0.5038 0.5038 0.0214 0.0040 0.3552 0.0133)
  ("free to contact us at permissions@oreilly.com." 0.1429 0.5160 0.5014 0.5229 0.5215 0.0214 0.0047 0.3496 0.0316)
